OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AAt least 64 killed in Spanish
OL,4,Ahigh-speed train crash with dozens
OL,5,Aseriously injured, regional government
OL,6,Asays
OL,7,
OL,8,FThe rail operator Iryo says its train
OL,9,Fwas "struck from behind" by a Renfe
OL,10,Ftrain. More than 500 passengers were
OL,11,Ftravelling on the two trains
OL,13,FSpain's Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez
OL,14,Fsays he is "shocked by the serious
OL,15,Ftrain accident" and is on his way to
OL,16,Fthe crash site
OL,18,FWitnesses have described "chaos" at the
OL,19,Fscene, while Roberto Gomez, a Spanish
OL,20,Fjournalist travelling on one of the
OL,21,Ftrains, says the "carriage is
OL,22,Fcompletely destroyed"
OL,23,APub: 28-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
